<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#"
     xml:base="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:fsdas="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:owl2xml="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/owl2-xml#"
     xmlns:specieshabitat="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#"
     xmlns:aquaticresources="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">to represent species together with their typical environment in terms of habitat and water area</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Specieshabitat Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>what species have what habitat in what water area?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>The pattern allows to represent species with a typical habitat and a typical water area where the exemplars can be found. However, there is no direct relation between the habitat (type) and the water area; in principle, it is possible that there are no places in the water area that provide the conditions for that habitat.
In order to represent that a species has a habitat within a given water area, the situation pattern should be reused and specialized, as in the speciesconditions.owl pattern.</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">to represent species together with their typical environment in terms of habitat and water area</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>speciesconditions.owl</cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>give me the species having a &apos;demersal&apos; habitat in water area &apos;24&apos;</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label removed x1; label added x11; term declared x3;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Specieshabitat Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl&gt; as an individual, as pattern.ttl did
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>This pattern encodes a FSDAS competency question, with an indication to use some Species class, and some hasHabitat property, with range xsd:string.
Since the application task of FSDAS is to jointly query FIGIS factsheet data and RTMS time series data, the pattern must encode elements that can be easily mapped to FIGIS and RTMS schemas/ontologies.
Issue (1) mapping Species to FIGIS schema, since the needed schema elements are two instead of one.
Issue (2) representation of habitats in the pattern is intuitively with objects, since habitats are typically objects, and points in a value space (as the referents of xsd datatypes typically are). The suggestion in the competencey question is to use xsd.string though.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Specieshabitat Pattern</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>Created by Aldo Gangemi</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Annotation properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://purl.org/dc/terms/description -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/description">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Description (DC terms)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/dc/terms/title -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Title</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#coversRequirements -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#coversRequirements">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">covers requirements</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasConsequences -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasConsequences">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has consequences</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasIntent -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasIntent">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has intent</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#relatedCPs -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#relatedCPs">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">related c ps</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#scenarios -->

    <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#scenarios">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">scenarios</rdfs:label>
    </owl:AnnotationProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Object Properties
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasBottomType -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasBottomType">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#BottomType"/>
        <rdfs:label>hasBottomType</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasDepthZone -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasDepthZone">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#DepthZone"/>
        <rdfs:label>hasDepthZone</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasGeoform -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasGeoform">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Geoform"/>
        <rdfs:label>hasGeoForm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasHabitat -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasHabitat">
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#isHabitatFor"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticSpecies"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has habitat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#isHabitatFor -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#isHabitatFor">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticSpecies"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is habitat for</rdfs:label>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Classes
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticResource -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticResource">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasBottomType"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#BottomType"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasDepthZone"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#DepthZone"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasGeoform"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Geoform"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Aquatic resource</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticSpecies -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticSpecies">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#hasHabitat"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Here also the complex type SpeciesFeature (holding association with HabitatBio) is the schema mapping required to refer to Habitat. Any mapping has to take care of that, e.g. maps(AquaticSpecies, owl:unionOf(SpeciesRef, SpeciesFeature)).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Aquatic species</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#WaterArea -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#WaterArea">
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Water area</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#BottomType -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#BottomType">
        <rdfs:label>BottomType</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#DepthZone -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#DepthZone">
        <rdfs:label>DepthZone</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Geoform -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Geoform">
        <rdfs:label>Geoform</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#Habitat">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl#isHabitatFor"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#AquaticSpecies"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment>Habitat is the biological and ecological context of a species in the area of an aquatic resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Habitat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Individuals
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    


    <!-- http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl -->

    <owl:Thing rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/specieshabitat.owl">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    </owl:Thing>
</rdf:RDF>



